{"id": "EUVD-2026-82046", "enisaUuid": "82110e18-034d-3b9f-ae07-e0c99dc6647c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid1: create serial pool adding rdev to array with serialize_policy=1\n\nThe following bug has been observed with kernel 7.1.3 after adding a new\nrdev to an existing RAID1 array with serialize_policy enabled:\n\n  Oops: 0002 [#1]\n  CPU: 0 UID: 0 PID: 19639 Comm: ext4lazyinit Not tainted 7.1.3-1-default\n  RIP: _raw_spin_lock_irqsave+0x27/0x50\n  CR2: 0000000000004960\n  Call Trace:\n   wait_for_serialization+0xb9/0x260 [raid1]\n   raid1_make_request+0x762/0xaff [raid1]\n   md_handle_request+0x1c9/0x2e0 [md_mod]\n\nThe raid1.c code calls wait_for_serialization() if the MD_SERIALIZE_POLICY\nis set, and wait_for_serialization assumes that rdev->serial is\ninitialized. Normally this will be the case for arrays that have\nthe serialize_policy sysfs attribute set to 1.\n\nBut when a new rdev is added to an existing array in bind_rdev_to_array(),\nthe condition at mddev_create_serial_pool() causes creation of rdev->serial\nto be skipped. Fix it.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b187e14dab458d54425fc400f1e1e8d481d9bcf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9e4364449f7ca6917f3599eb32064dba5b7b147", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/37f11973c3eb72a5eb061082cad529bb6939c24f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c02d675e81468003e4f2253b616c53729070d712", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/140234b2380ffb8ffb0cfc46fee0e822f43adef7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6jq9-46p7-p377", "CVE-2026-90385"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04160530-c1e4-3b1a-a67e-6896a46ff6d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "124018da-d90d-33f2-9924-32193bf557fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69b00b5bb23552d43e8bbed73ef6624604bb94a2 <140234b2380ffb8ffb0cfc46fee0e822f43adef7"}, {"id": "1b1d3741-004e-3b97-8a18-444daa9c9908", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "527a701e-9a01-376b-a3dd-b4807f1120b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "5aece75f-2167-37c8-bc41-ff37d9520910", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69b00b5bb23552d43e8bbed73ef6624604bb94a2 <c02d675e81468003e4f2253b616c53729070d712"}, {"id": "5ce95813-f006-3037-8be0-75117b843491", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "65dd6052-0e9d-340b-afe4-f1e0dc22209b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7ff9c51a-d6ad-3315-b80b-cdb6730cb3b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "8499ac97-030f-3ac4-946a-69eb4526ca80", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "b56a72db-7206-39ce-84db-ef30232ce0eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69b00b5bb23552d43e8bbed73ef6624604bb94a2 <0b187e14dab458d54425fc400f1e1e8d481d9bcf"}, {"id": "f528e6d7-3e79-3c20-af2d-49918ec640cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69b00b5bb23552d43e8bbed73ef6624604bb94a2 <f9e4364449f7ca6917f3599eb32064dba5b7b147"}, {"id": "fd2ccd47-b05d-35c6-8a3b-43beffc12b61", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "69b00b5bb23552d43e8bbed73ef6624604bb94a2 <37f11973c3eb72a5eb061082cad529bb6939c24f"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "48336edd-c8fd-313e-a63b-ad964e323a40", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}